KG42.register("rules-c64e2b644dd347223d892867",{"id":"04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R003","paper":"04-energy_collectives","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R003","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The community manager is responsible for interfacing with the market and system operator and guaranteeing collective common agreements. Scope: Community-manager responsibilities in the energy collective. Different community agreements are incorporated through changes to the community-manager model without modifying prosumer models. Scope: Introducing different collective common agreements. Condition: When different community agreements are incorporated into the market model. The non-profit community manager aims to minimize the modelled costs associated with internal common agreements and its interface with the market or system operator. Scope: Community-manager objective in the equilibrium formulation.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Community-manager objective in the equilibrium formulation. | Community-manager responsibilities in the energy collective. | Introducing different collective common agreements.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g03-E17"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-qimp","symbol":"q_imp","meaning":"Total energy imported by the community from the system operator; a global variable of the community-manager interface model g.","kind":"operational","domain":"Continuous energy quantity. In the community-manager problem (19), q_imp is constrained by −q_imp ≤ 0, i.e. q_imp ≥ 0. Further bounds are not specified in the supplied evidence for this coordination rule.","unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g03-E17"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-qexp","symbol":"q_exp","meaning":"Total energy exported by the community to the system operator; a global variable of the community-manager interface model g.","kind":"operational","domain":"Continuous energy quantity. In the community-manager problem (19), q_exp is constrained by −q_exp ≤ 0, i.e. q_exp ≥ 0. Further bounds are not specified in the supplied evidence for this coordination rule.","unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g03-E17"]}],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The community manager is responsible for interfacing with the market and system operator and guaranteeing collective common agreements. Scope: Community-manager responsibilities in the energy collective.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E11"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Different community agreements are incorporated through changes to the community-manager model without modifying prosumer models. Scope: Introducing different collective common agreements. Condition: When different community agreements are incorporated into the market model.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The non-profit community manager aims to minimize the modelled costs associated with internal common agreements and its interface with the market or system operator. Scope: Community-manager objective in the equilibrium formulation.","expression":"min_{Γ} g(q_imp, q_imp)   (19a)\ns.t.  − q_imp ≤ 0   (γ_i)   (19b)\n      − q_exp ≤ 0   (γ_e)   (19c)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-qimp","v141-c-R003-x-qexp"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E17"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p01-c1r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":"3994","section":"Abstract and Nomenclature","anchor_text":"3994 IE Energy Collectives: A Co Based Approach to Futu Fabio Moret and Pierre Pinson Abstract—While","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"This work introduces the concept of energy collectives, as a community-based electricity market structure. We find that when prosumers are allowed to share energy at community level, the overall electricity procurement for the community reflects prosumers' preferences. We show that community members can be influenced by a supervisory third-party in charge of interfacing with the market and system operator and of guaranteeing the collective common agreements."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":"3996","section":"II. Energy Collectives and Their Operational Framework","anchor_text":"αj, βj ≥0 , j = 1, . . . , n (1g) where Γ = {pj, qj, αj, βj} is the set of decision variables and qi","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The core of this market organization is the inclusion, in the negotiation process, of common agreements on how the energy collective is to jointly handle its internal objectives and its interaction with the outside world. We address this role to the community manager and we model it in (1) by means of the function g. We define g only by global variables (q_imp and q_exp) and by a set of relevant parameters or additionally variables theta. Different community agreements can be included only by operating on the community manager, without modifying the prosumers model."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p10-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":10,"printed_page":"4003","section":"Appendix","anchor_text":"ESS BASED APPROACH TO FUTURE ELECTRICITY MARKETS 4003 in the market operator. At the same time, the ","equation_id":"(19)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"the market operator. At the same time, the community manager, since non-profit, aims for the minimization of the costs related to internal common agreements and interface with market or system operator. It follows that\nmin_{Γ} g(q_imp, q_imp)   (19a)\ns.t.  − q_imp ≤ 0   (γ_i)   (19b)\n      − q_exp ≤ 0   (γ_e)   (19c)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p01-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":"3994","section":"Abstract and Nomenclature","anchor_text":"Only the most important symbols of this paper are included. αj Energy imported by prosumer j. βj Ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Only the most important symbols of this paper are included. alpha_j Energy imported by prosumer j. beta_j Energy exported by prosumer j. delta_j Upper bound of alpha_j. gamma Penalization coefficient (the subscript identifies the specific application). lambda_j Price of energy perceived by prosumer j. lambda_DA Day-ahead market price. P_j Feasible space of p_j. R_j Feasible space of prosumer j. U_ij Feasible space of u_ij. U-upper_ij Upper bound of asset i of prosumer j. psi_ij Cost/utility function of asset i of prosumer j. rho Penalization factor of L_rho. tau Price spread between import and export price. f-tilde_j Extended cost function of prosumer j. U-lower_ij Lower bound of asset i of prosumer j. c_ij Quadratic coefficient of psi_ij. d_ij Linear coefficient of psi_ij. f_j Cost function of prosumer j. g Model of community manager. h_j Preferences and/or transaction costs of prosumer j. I_j Set of assets of prosumer j. L_rho Augmented Lagrangian. n Number of prosumers in the collective. N_j Set of members of neighbourhood j. p_j Net energy produced by prosumer j. q_j Energy imported by prosumer j from the community. q_exp Total energy exported. q_imp Total energy imported. r_k Vector of primal residuals. s_k Vector of dual residuals. u_ij Power set-point of asset i of prosumer j. v_ij Energy traded between neighbourhood i and j. y Vector of Lagrangian multipliers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":"3996","section":"II. Energy Collectives and Their Operational Framework","anchor_text":"as the solution of the exchange problem ad n of min fj(pj, qj, αj, βj) + g(qimp, qexp, ϑ) (1a) ap Γ ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The optimal community dispatch is then obtained as the solution of the exchange problem: min_{Gamma} sum_{j=1}^{n} f_j(p_j, q_j, alpha_j, beta_j) + g(q_imp, q_exp, theta)   (1a)  s.t. p_j + q_j + alpha_j - beta_j = 0 , j = 1, . . . , n   (1b)  sum_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0   (1c)  sum_{j=1}^{n} alpha_j = q_imp   (1d)  sum_{j=1}^{n} beta_j = q_exp   (1e)  p_j in P_j , j = 1, . . . , n   (1f)  alpha_j, beta_j >= 0 , j = 1, . . . , n   (1g)  where Gamma = {p_j, q_j, alpha_j, beta_j} is the set of decision variables and q_imp, q_exp are continuous variables describing import and export exchanges with the system operator."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":"The supplied evidence defines g as depending on the global variables q_imp and q_exp and on an abstract set of relevant parameters or additional variables theta (v141-b-g01-E11). However, equation (19) and the coordination rule fix no concrete parameter, coefficient, or theta member for this community-manager objective, so no parameter objects are declared for this rule. This does not assert that the source lacks parameters in other interface models or in the full formulation (1)."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M02-coordination"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","quote":"a supervisory third-party in charge of interfacing with the market and system operator and of guaranteeing the collective common agreements."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","quote":"The core of this market organization is the inclusion, in the negotiation process, of common agreements on how the energy collective is to jointly handle its internal objectives and its interaction with the outside world. We address this role to the community manager and we model it in (1) by means of the function g."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","quote":"Different community agreements can be included only by operating on the community manager, without modifying the prosumers model."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E17","quote":"At the same time, the community manager, since non-profit, aims for the minimization of the costs related to internal common agreements and interface with market or system operator."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"9b32269ba163d40edd3e58a5c681f625ca6a6a2e7274b3590166d9802b699686","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Equation (19) in v141-b-g03-E17 supplies a source-supported mathematical objective for the community-manager coordination constraint C003: min_{Γ} g(q_imp, q_imp) subject to −q_imp ≤ 0 and −q_exp ≤ 0. C001 and C002 remain procedural and not_formalized because they state responsibilities and model-change conventions rather than mathematical expressions. The frozen graph has only the node coordination.local_operator and no edges; C.2 therefore attaches the declared interface variables and the formalized objective constraint to that existing node without changing V, E, mechanism, market, or rule identity.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-x-qimp","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"q_imp is a global interface variable of the community-manager objective g formalized in (19a). The frozen node coordination.local_operator is the graph object that carries the community-manager coordination function; no edge is needed for a variable that is an argument of that node's objective."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-x-qexp","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"q_exp is a global interface variable constrained in the community-manager problem (19c). It is attached to the frozen node coordination.local_operator, the community-manager coordination object identified by this rule, with no graph edge asserted beyond that membership."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Equation (19) identifies g, the community-manager model, as the objective minimized by the non-profit community manager subject to non-negativity of q_imp and q_exp. This formalized constraint is bound to the only frozen node for this rule, coordination.local_operator; the frozen graph provides no additional edges for this unary objective constraint."}],"revision_requests":["Confirm the argument list of equation (19a): the supplied source_text prints g(q_imp, q_imp). The same duplicated second argument appears in (16a), while other formulations print g(q_imp, q_exp). Determine whether the second argument in (19a) is intentionally q_imp or is a source typo for q_exp.","Clarify the minimization variable set Γ in (19): in (1) Γ is defined as {p_j, q_j, α_j, β_j}, while q_imp and q_exp are described as separate continuous variables. The supplied evidence for (19) does not state whether q_imp and q_exp belong to Γ in the community-manager minimization; this affects the formal domain of the minimization and should be resolved by source-aware review.","The frozen graph contains only coordination.local_operator and has no variable nodes or edges for this rule. C.2 has attached q_imp and q_exp to the existing node. If the graph template requires explicit variable nodes or edges to represent the interface variables of equation (19), C.1 should add them; otherwise the current binding is sufficient for the rule-level objective."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
